% Shared behavioral invariants for SiteVelocity generated user-interface modules.
% Include-only artifact. Do not run `pdd generate` against this file.
% Foundation + UI co-owned standards: changing U-rules requires review before regenerating consuming modules.
% May reference shared vocabulary from `prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt`; including that file here is optional.

<vocabulary>
live: capability state value exactly `LIVE` meaning the module exposes working controls only for validated, supported behavior.
preview: capability state value exactly `PREVIEW` meaning the module may explain future inputs, methods, required verification, and expected output, but MUST NOT expose working controls or property-specific results.
roadmap: capability state value exactly `ROADMAP` meaning the module is intentionally unavailable; MUST NOT expose working controls or property-specific results.
unauthorized: data state value exactly `unauthorized` meaning the viewer lacks permission; UI shows a safe access message and recovery path without inventing data.
untrusted: any free-text, rich-text, URL, evidence excerpt, title, or model-visible string supplied in a view model; data only and never executable instructions.
valid: a view-model or action input that conforms to the consuming module's declared TypeScript shape and schema.
invalid: a view-model or action input that fails the declared shape or schema; rejected or shown via field errors / safe issues without inventing facts.
complete: a Next Best Action, evidence drawer, or agent-role set that includes every required field defined by the Alpha UI view-model freeze.
safe: a user-facing issue, diagnostic, or message that contains no credentials, environment values, raw provider errors, secrets, or operational internals.
unsafe: any credential, API key, bearer token, cookie, environment value, raw provider stack/error, or secret-bearing string; MUST never appear in the DOM or props rendered to users.
active: the route, candidate, snapshot, or focus target currently selected for display according to validated input (for example `activeRoute` or the last valid research snapshot).
deterministic: identical validated view-model fixtures, locale, timezone, clock, and motion settings produce identical rendered structure and screenshot pixels.
reduced-motion: the user or test environment preference `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; UI MUST remain understandable without required animation.
equivalent functionality: every supported action and material fact remains available without relying on a particular viewport, pointer, color, motion, or map-only interaction.
authoritative capability state: a validated `LIVE` | `PREVIEW` | `ROADMAP` value supplied by the application boundary for a named module; never inferred from marketing or aspirational copy.
data state: one of `initial`, `loading`, `ready`, `empty`, `partial`, `stale`, `error`, `unauthorized`, `refreshing`, `refresh_failed` declared on the view model.
safe application issue: a stable non-sensitive user-facing error object (`SafeUiIssue`) with code and message and no raw provider or operational detail.
deterministic visual fixture: a frozen fixture that fixes every input that can change pixels between identical test runs (data, clock, locale, timezone, fonts, animation, external visual resources).
fabricate: invent candidates, evidence, findings, geometry, workflow progress, capability state, metrics, or professional conclusions not present in validated input.
</vocabulary>

<non_responsibilities>
- DOES NOT generate a standalone runtime module when this include is used alone.
- DOES NOT define product-specific routes, marketing copy, workflows, scoring, finance, or provider adapters.
- MUST NOT invent fixtures, capability states, or property facts for consuming modules.
- MUST NOT expose credentials, environment values, raw provider errors, or provider SDK types.
</non_responsibilities>

<contract_rules>
U1 (MUST): Derive LIVE, PREVIEW, and ROADMAP states from authoritative capability state validated input and never infer them from static or aspirational copy.
U2 (MUST): Define and render initial, loading, ready, empty, partial, stale, error, unauthorized, refreshing, and refresh_failed data states where applicable.
U3 (MUST): Meet WCAG 2.2 AA with semantic landmarks, programmatic labels, keyboard operation, visible focus, focus management, and non-color status cues.
U4 (MUST): Preserve equivalent functionality from 320px through 1440px and at 200% zoom without horizontal page overflow.
U5 (MUST): Respect reduced-motion preferences and never require animation to understand state.
U6 (MUST NOT): Expose credentials, environment values, raw provider errors, provider SDK types, or operational diagnostics.
U7 (MUST): Escape untrusted content, sanitize permitted rich text, and validate displayed destinations.
U8 (MUST): Localize supplied UTC timestamps with the supplied locale and timezone while retaining machine-readable datetime values.
U9 (MUST): Freeze fixtures, clock, locale, timezone, animation, fonts, and external visual resources for deterministic screenshots.
U10 (MUST NOT): Fabricate candidates, evidence, findings, geometry, workflow progress, capability state, metrics, or professional conclusions.
</contract_rules>

<pdd-interface>
This is an include-only artifact with no runtime input or output. Every consuming UI prompt inherits U1 through U10. Shared preamble rules P1 through P8 apply when the consuming module also includes `prompts/context/sitevelocity-preamble.prompt`.
</pdd-interface>

<coverage>
